      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-flow\u0022\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-article\u0022\u003E\n  \u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\n  \u003Cp class=\u0022public-copy\u0022\u003EHead of Technology at Corporate LinX, hands-on software architect and creator of cCoder. Paul works across architecture, delivery and operations, connecting technical choices to business consequences.\u003C/p\u003E\n  \u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-actions\u0022\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-primary\u0022 href=\u0022https://www.linkedin.com/in/paul-ward-136bb724/\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-share\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EConnect on LinkedIn\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-secondary\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-source-code\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EView the code\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-article\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EExpertise built across the whole lifecycle\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPaul has 27 years of commercial C# and .NET experience and two decades building cloud applications. His work spans application and data architecture, Azure migration, platform rebuilds, systems integration, engineering standards, operational support, audit readiness and the practical work of helping teams deliver. At Corporate LinX he progressed into the Head of Technology role and became the senior technical point of accountability between engineering and the CEO. He remains hands-on because credible leadership depends on understanding how the system behaves, where risk accumulates and what a proposed change will demand in production.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2\u003EValues visible in the decisions\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EProtect the business outcome first.\u003C/strong\u003E During an incident, restore the essential service and protect affected people before optimising the technical response. \u003Cstrong\u003EBuild the factual picture.\u003C/strong\u003E Bring together the people who know each part of the process, follow evidence and resist the comfort of the first plausible answer. \u003Cstrong\u003ELeave the system stronger.\u003C/strong\u003E A repair is incomplete without root-cause understanding, regression coverage and better detection or operational guidance. \u003Cstrong\u003ECreate clarity that others can use.\u003C/strong\u003E Architecture should help engineers and decision-makers act with confidence. It should not depend on the architect remaining the only person who understands it.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section \u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-grid\u0022\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-card\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2 class=\u0022public-card-title\u0022\u003ERebuilding a B2B financial-services platform\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA business-critical platform needed new commercial capability, reliable integration and a stronger cloud operating model. Paul held technical accountability across its rebuild, Azure migration, architecture, delivery practice, operations and audit readiness.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-card\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2 class=\u0022public-card-title\u0022\u003EProtecting supplier payments through failure\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAn obscure transaction-path defect threatened a supply-chain-finance payment process. The response protected supplier payment first, then established root cause, added regression coverage and strengthened detection around the failure path.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-card\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2 class=\u0022public-card-title\u0022\u003EMaking AI exploration inspectable\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFor a US legal-education publisher, Paul developed prototypes around content ingestion, audiobook workflows and assessment concepts\u2014turning broad possibilities into working approaches without overstating their production maturity.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-article\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy cCoder exists\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EcCoder is a place to develop architectural ideas in working software. The platform provides a real codebase in which principles can be tested against APIs, persistence, background services, deployment and maintenance.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section \u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-grid\u0022\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-card\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2 class=\u0022public-card-title\u0022\u003EArchitectural method\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA practical adoption of The Standard across a family of .NET domain systems.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-card-action\u0022\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/The-Standard-in-cCoder\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-source-code\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003ERead the article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-card\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2 class=\u0022public-card-title\u0022\u003EExplore cCoder\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESee the systems used to test those architectural ideas in working software.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-card-action\u0022\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/Platform-Domains\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-grid-layout\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003ERead the article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-card\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2 class=\u0022public-card-title\u0022\u003EBusiness perspective\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECore systems are valuable when they improve operational truth, control and recoverability.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-card-action\u0022\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022/The-Value-of-Core-Business-Systems\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-arrow-right\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003ERead the article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      },
