        "Html": "\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-flow\u0022\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-article public-domain-article\u0022\u003E\n  \u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\n  \u003Cp class=\u0022public-copy\u0022\u003EGive applications one governed way to select and run inference providers without coupling business workflows to a vendor.\u003C/p\u003E\n  \u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-actions\u0022\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-primary\u0022 href=\u0022/Platform-Domains\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-grid-layout\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EAll platform domains\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-secondary\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.AI\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-source-code\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EView the GitHub repository\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-secondary\u0022 href=\u0022/Documentation/AI\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-file\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003ERead the documentation\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-article public-domain-article\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat it owns\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENamed providers for Ollama, OpenAI, Foundry and Codex.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECompletion, agent orchestration and model-capability services.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPer-provider concurrency limits, transient retry handling and capability-driven model discovery.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy the boundary matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EApplications can choose the right inference boundary for a workload while retaining explicit provider configuration, operational limits and deterministic business control around probabilistic output.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EHow it fits\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAI is a key adjacent domain and is already consumed by the CRM application. It is not yet included in cCoder.Core, but is expected to join the composition when its independent provider abstraction and reuse boundary are ready for wider platform use.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGetting started\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe source, current README, sample hosts and tests live in \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.AI\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003EcCoder.AI on GitHub\u003C/a\u003E. The repository README is the version-specific starting point; the outline below explains how the pieces fit together.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EReference the package\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-xml\u0022\u003E\u0026lt;PackageReference Include=\u0022cCoder.AI\u0022 Version=\u0022YOUR_VERSION\u0022 /\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EDuring coordinated local development the repositories may substitute a sibling \u003Ccode\u003EProjectReference\u003C/code\u003E. Published applications should normally consume the agreed package version so the dependency boundary remains explicit.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003ERegister it in the host\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003Ebuilder.Services.AddAI(ai =\u0026gt;\u0026#10;{\u0026#10;    ai.DefaultProvider = \u0022local\u0022;\u0026#10;    ai.AddOllama(\u0022local\u0022, p =\u0026gt;\u0026#10;    {\u0026#10;        p.Endpoint = \u0022http://localhost:11434\u0022;\u0026#10;        p.Model = \u0022qwen3.5:4b\u0022;\u0026#10;        p.MaxConcurrency = 1;\u0026#10;    });\u0026#10;});\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EConfigure and run it\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ERegister each Ollama, OpenAI, Foundry or Codex endpoint once under a stable provider key. Store API keys outside source control, set provider concurrency deliberately, and configure retry behaviour for transient 408, 429 and 5xx responses.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EConsume the capability\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EInject \u003Ccode\u003EICompletionProviderService\u003C/code\u003E for completion requests or \u003Ccode\u003EIAgentOrchestrationService\u003C/code\u003E for agent runs, passing the provider key when the default is not appropriate. Query \u003Ccode\u003EIModelManagerService\u003C/code\u003E before offering model selection.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EBuild and verify from source\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-powershell\u0022\u003Egit clone https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.AI.git\ncd cCoder.AI\ndotnet build\ndotnet test\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EUse the repository-specific solution and test commands from its README when working on the domain itself; the standalone and acceptance-test hosts show the supported application boundary more accurately than an isolated snippet can.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
