        "CultureId": "en-GB",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-flow\u0022\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-article public-domain-article\u0022\u003E\n  \u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\n  \u003Cp class=\u0022public-copy\u0022\u003ETurn operational evidence into an app-aware capability that can be queried, streamed and retained deliberately.\u003C/p\u003E\n  \u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-actions\u0022\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-primary\u0022 href=\u0022/Platform-Domains\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-grid-layout\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EAll platform domains\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-secondary\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.Logging\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-source-code\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EView the GitHub repository\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-secondary\u0022 href=\u0022/Documentation/Logging\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-file\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003ERead the documentation\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\n\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection class=\u0022public-flow-section public-section\u0022\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-section-frame\u0022\u003E\u003Carticle class=\u0022public-article public-domain-article\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat it owns\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EDB-backed ILogger provider and OData read/post endpoints.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EApplication-scoped log records with attached data.\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESignalR streaming and scheduled retention cleanup.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy the boundary matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESupport and engineering teams get a shared record of system behaviour without giving public callers permission to rewrite history.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EHow it fits\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe domain is published and tested independently, then composed through cCoder.Core when an application needs the complete platform. That keeps ownership visible while preserving a straightforward application bootstrap.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGetting started\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe source, current README, sample hosts and tests live in \u003Ca href=\u0022https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.Logging\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003EcCoder.Logging on GitHub\u003C/a\u003E. The repository README is the version-specific starting point; the outline below explains how the pieces fit together.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EReference the package\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-xml\u0022\u003E\u0026lt;PackageReference Include=\u0022cCoder.Logging\u0022 Version=\u0022YOUR_VERSION\u0022 /\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EDuring coordinated local development the repositories may substitute a sibling \u003Ccode\u003EProjectReference\u003C/code\u003E. Published applications should normally consume the agreed package version so the dependency boundary remains explicit.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003ERegister it in the host\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003Ebuilder.Services.AddLoggingWeb(/* platform configuration */);\u0026#10;app.StartLoggingWeb();\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EConfigure and run it\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EConfigure Core persistence, application identity, the logging API route and retention policy. Use the HostedServices registration when scheduled retention cleanup runs in a worker process.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EConsume the capability\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWrite through the supplied \u003Ccode\u003EILogger\u003C/code\u003E provider, query application-scoped LogEntry records through OData, and use SignalR streaming for live operational views. Attach structured LogDataItem values rather than hiding evidence in formatted strings.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EBuild and verify from source\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-powershell\u0022\u003Egit clone https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.Logging.git\ncd cCoder.Logging\ndotnet build\ndotnet test\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EUse the repository-specific solution and test commands from its README when working on the domain itself; the standalone and acceptance-test hosts show the supported application boundary more accurately than an isolated snippet can.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
