e Web host.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EConsume the capability\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAuthenticate through the account/session boundary, then use the Security OData sets such as \u003Ccode\u003ESSOUser\u003C/code\u003E, \u003Ccode\u003ETenant\u003C/code\u003E and \u003Ccode\u003EUserEvent\u003C/code\u003E. Subscribe to account lifecycle events instead of copying SSO state directly.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EBuild and verify from source\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-powershell\u0022\u003Egit clone https://github.com/ccoder-co-uk/cCoder.Security.git\ncd cCoder.Security\ndotnet build\ndotnet test\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EUse the repository-specific solution and test commands from its README when working on the domain itself; the standalone and acceptance-test hosts show the supported application boundary more accurately than an isolated snippet can.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/article\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
