        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing App Security Management \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou this functionality through the App Management Tabs. From the Security tab you can manage\n        multiple things, including what roles exist in the system \u0026amp; what particular tasks they can carry out within the\n        portal.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you access the security tab, you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/SecurityTab-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis grid shows the bare minimum amount of roles that are required for our system and they\n        determine what can be viewed/interacted with in a particular scenario. For example if you\u0026rsquo;re not logged in\n        (guest), the access you have is massively limited. If you\u0026rsquo;re a new user (users) then you have access to more\n        than a guest would have, however this is still limited to what privileges you\u0026rsquo;ve been granted as a user. And of\n        course, administrators have a lot more privileges than normal users do. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExpanding the users one gives you another grid that looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/UsersTab-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWithin this expanded view, you can manage what users are in each role and remove them from the\n        roles if necessary. You will also see that there is a Privileges tab in this expanded view, this is a way to\n        control each of the roles and what actions they can carry out. As an example (see the following screenshot),\n        users are only able to \u0026ldquo;read\u0026rdquo; (view) apps and are unable to create, update and delete them as those are tasks\n        that can only be carried out by admins in this case. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/PrivilegesTab-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESelecting which privileges should be applied to a role is done simply by just selecting the\n        appropriate boxes on the appropriate grid rows.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAdding a User to a Role \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThere are two ways in which you can add a user to a role, the first way is to click the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Add User By Id\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Ebutton which will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/AddUserByIdDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022227\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIn here, you must enter the user\u0026rsquo;s Id into the text box and press confirm. If the user\u0026rsquo;s Id is\n        unknown to you, then you can click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Add Users\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button that will bring up a dialog that\n        looks something\n        like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/AddUsersDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022577\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere you must find the user you wish to add to the role. If you click the filter buttons at the\n        top of the columns, you can search for a specific user which will make it easier to add them to the role you\n        wish to. For example, to add User 12345 to the User\u0026rsquo;s role here you would select the top row and then click the\n        confirm button. This will then grant the user the privileges associated with that role.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ECreating a Role \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo create a new role in this UI, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New Role\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button in the\n        header bar. Clicking this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/CreateRoleDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022197\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECreating a Role is incredibly simple, only requiring you to add a name to it. Once you\u0026rsquo;ve\n        filled in this field and clicked confirm, your new role will now exist in the system. You can then begin\n        applying specific privileges to it and add users to it.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/TestRole-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFor now, I have created a test role to demonstrate how a new one would look within the existing\n        list.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpdating a Role \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou can edit the name you\u0026rsquo;ve given to your role by just clicking on it within the grid:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/UpdateRole-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOnce you\u0026rsquo;ve made any changes you want, you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Save\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button on the\n        corresponding grid row and any changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made will be saved.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EDeleting a Role \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a role that you no longer want or need then you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Delete\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button that will\n        remove your role and from the our system.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Security/DeleteRole-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      },
