        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cstyle class=\u0022code-analysis-syntax\u0022\u003E\n.docs-content pre{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0 1.75rem;padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border:1px solid rgba(20,42,72,.16);border-left:4px solid #0e6fae;border-radius:4px;background:#f7fbfe;color:#10263a}\n.docs-content pre code{white-space:pre;color:inherit;background:transparent;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.65}\n.language-csharp .syntax-comment{color:#587287;font-style:italic}.language-csharp .syntax-string{color:#8a3d12}.language-csharp .syntax-keyword{color:#6542a6;font-weight:700}.language-csharp .syntax-number{color:#096b65}.language-csharp .syntax-type{color:#0a6680;font-weight:600}\n\u003C/style\u003E\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAn API acceptance suite must cover Get, Post, Put, and Delete operations.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022public-actions docs-rule-actions\u0022\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-primary\u0022 href=\u0022/Documentation/CodeAnalysis/STXTEST\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-arrow-left\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003EBack to STXTEST rules\u003C/a\u003E\u003Ca class=\u0022btn btn-secondary\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/hassanhabib/The-Standard\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noreferrer\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022k-icon k-i-book\u0022\u003E\u003C/span\u003ERead The Standard source\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/div\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat The Standard says\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAn API acceptance suite must cover Get, Post, Put, and Delete operations. The analyser reports this as a warning at the declaration or statement that needs attention.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhy it matters\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis rule belongs to the Tests family. Following it keeps responsibilities and intent visible to readers, tooling and future maintainers.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EBad code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Violates STXTEST006: An API acceptance suite must cover Get, Post, Put, and Delete operations.\u003C/span\u003E\n\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Acceptance suite covers only Get and Post.\u003C/span\u003E\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EGood code example\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode class=\u0022language-csharp\u0022\u003E\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-comment\u0022\u003E// Follows STXTEST006\u003C/span\u003E\n[\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EFact\u003C/span\u003E] \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EShouldGet\u003C/span\u003E() =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\n[\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EFact\u003C/span\u003E] \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EShouldPost\u003C/span\u003E() =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\n[\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EFact\u003C/span\u003E] \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EShouldPut\u003C/span\u003E() =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\n[\u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EFact\u003C/span\u003E] \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EValueTask\u003C/span\u003E \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-type\u0022\u003EShouldDelete\u003C/span\u003E() =\u0026gt; \u003Cspan class=\u0022syntax-keyword\u0022\u003Edefault\u003C/span\u003E;\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E"
      }
    ],
    "PageInfo": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Description": "An API acceptance suite must cover Get, Post, Put, and Delete operations.",
        "Title": "STXTEST006"
      }
    ]
  },
