        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing Layout Management\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou Access this page through the App Management Tabs. From here you can manage the app\u0026rsquo;s\n            layout, where you can alter the app\u0026rsquo;s logos and their placements and you can manage their sites navigation\n            bar styles.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you access the layouts tab, you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Layouts/LayoutsGrid-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis grid contains any relevant layouts, which can be set on a page-by-page basis, for\n            example, the documentation pages you\u0026rsquo;re looking at right now will have a different layout to the app\u0026rsquo;s home\n            page.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ECreating a Layout\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo create a new layout in this UI, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New Layout\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button\n            in the header bar.\n            Clicking this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Layouts/CreateLayoutDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022154\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECreating a Layout in our system is incredibly simple \u0026amp; only requires you to give it a name.\n            The name should be relevant to what the layout is going to be used for. Once you\u0026rsquo;ve filled in the field, you\n            can press create and create your new layout.\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Layouts/CreatedLayout-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFor now, I have created a Test layout. On this row you can see that there are save and\n            delete functions and there\u0026rsquo;s the ability expand the component.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpdating a Layout \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOn expanding a new layout, you will come across 2 boxes in which you can implement your\n            layout. In the header box, you will typically find any required\n            \u003Cmeta /\u003Eand\n \u003Clink /\u003Etags for any pages that use that particular layout. In the body box, it\u0026rsquo;s a simple breakdown of the\n            page layout - header, body and footer and all of the page\u0026rsquo;s content get\u0026rsquo;s populated into the page\u0026rsquo;s body.\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Layouts/UpdateLayoutContent-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo save any changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made within a layout you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Save\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button\n            on the relevant\n            row. This will save any changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made to this layout.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EDeleting a Layout \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a layout that you no longer use or need, then you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Delete\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button that\n            will remove your layout and its content from the UI.\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Layouts/DeleteLayout-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
    ],
    "PageInfo": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Description": "How to access and manage the layouts in the portal.",
        "Title": "Layouts"
      }
    ],
    "ResourceKey": "Default"
  },
  {
    "Path": "Documentation/ContentManagement/AppManagement/Resources",
    "Name": "Resources",
    "ShowOnMenus": true,
    "Order": 50,
    "LastUpdated": "2026-07-21T17:12:43.0453555\u002B01:00",
    "Layout": "Documentation",
    "Contents": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing Resource Management\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou Access this page through the App Management Tabs. From here you can manage any resources\n            that are specific to the app that you\u0026rsquo;re working in. This should have a very limited number of resources in\n            it as the majority are Common Cached.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you access the resources tab, you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/ResourcesGrid-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere you can see the limited number of resources within our demo app, this is because the\n            vast majority of them are in the common cache which essentially means that they need to exist in every\n            portal we create. You will find that the minimal ones here are specific to this app only. When you expand a\n            row in the UI, it allows you to see the translations for that particular resource:\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/ResourceExpand-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWithin this particular piece of UI, it allows you to manage the translations for the\n            resource.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ECreating a Resource\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo create a new resource in this UI, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New Resource\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\n button in the header\n            bar. Clicking this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/CreateResourceDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022322\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere, \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Key\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is the \u0026ldquo;group\u0026rdquo; essentially that this resources fits in, this is\n            used by a\n            component to define what group of resources are used within it. When using a resource within a component or\n            a page, you must use our tags \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;[resource_displayname[blah]]\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Efor example, here, the\n            \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Name\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E would be filled\n            in as \u0026ldquo;blah\u0026rdquo;. The fields \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Display Name\u0026rdquo;, \u0026ldquo;Short Display Name\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and\n            \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Description\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E are used to define how you\n            want it to be displayed within the portal. for example you may want your \u0026ldquo;blah\u0026rdquo; resource to have a capital B\n            so you would fill the display name field in as \u0026ldquo;Blah\u0026rdquo;. If you don\u0026rsquo;t want them to have a different short\n            display name or an in depth description, then you need to fill all three fields with your chosen value. Once\n            you\u0026rsquo;ve filled your fields with your desired resource values, click confirm, this will create it and it will\n            then be visible in the UI. Creating the example blah resource returns the following in the UI.\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/CreatedResource-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ECreating a Translation for a Resource\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you expand this new resource you see that there are no translations that exists for it\n            just yet:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/ResourceExpandCreate-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo create a translation for this resource, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New\n Translation\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button.\n            Clicking this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/CreateTranslationDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022153\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWithin this dialog, you select the culture you wish to create the translation for, on\n            clicking create this will create a row in the translations grid that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/CreateTranslation-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis creates a French translation row in the table, you can understand how to alter the\n            values in the \u0026ldquo;Updating a Resource\u0026rdquo; section of this page.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpdating a Resource\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo update the resource you have created, perhaps there\u0026rsquo;s a typo or you want to change what\n            appears in the UI, you have to click on the text you want to change which will allow you to change the text\n            within it. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/UpdateResource-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo save the changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made, you must click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Save\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button on the\n            row relevant to the resource you\u0026rsquo;re changing.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EUpdating a Translation for a Resource\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIn order to alter a translation for a resource, you expand the resource you\u0026rsquo;re interested in\n            and click onto the content you wish to alter, this makes it editable.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/UpdateTranslation-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EChange the content of the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Display Name\u0026rdquo;, \u0026ldquo;Short Display Name\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Description\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E to the appropriate French translation and save it by clicking the save button within the translation row in the UI.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EDeleting a Resource \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a resource that you no longer use or need, then you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Delete\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button that will remove your resource and its content from the UI.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/DeleteResource-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EDeleting a Translation for a Resource\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a translation resource that you no longer use or need, then you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Delete\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button that will remove that particular translation and its content from the UI.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Resources/DeleteTranslation-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
    ],
    "PageInfo": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Description": "How to access and manage the resources in the portal.",
        "Title": "Resources"
      }
    ],
    "ResourceKey": "Default"
  },
  {
    "Path": "Documentation/ContentManagement/AppManagement/Templates",
    "Name": "Templates",
    "ShowOnMenus": true,
    "Order": 60,
    "LastUpdated": "2026-07-21T17:12:48.8578821\u002B01:00",
    "Layout": "Documentation",
    "Contents": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing Template Management\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou Access this page through the App Management Tabs. From here you can manage the app\u0026rsquo;s\n            template, managing things like the colour things appear \u0026amp; any CSS changes that need to happen within the\n            app,\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you access the templates tab, you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Templates/TemplatesGrid-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis grid contains any relevant templates for the given app, the most commonly used one\n            across all portals is the Theme-Default, which can be customised to ensure that our theming matches the\n            client\u0026rsquo;s requested theme.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ECreating a Template\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo create a new template in this UI, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New Template\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button\n            in the header bar. Clicking this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Templates/CreateTemplateDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022208\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere, \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Resource Key\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Eis the way that the system selects which resources to\n            use in this\n            template. For example, a domain key selects the resources published for that domain.\n            \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Name\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\n is the name you want your template to have that should be related to the places it will be used. Once you\u0026rsquo;ve\n            filled these text boxes in with the relevant information, you can press confirm to create your new template.\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Templates/CreatedTemplate-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFor now, I have created a Test template. On this row you can see that there are save and\n            delete functions and there\u0026rsquo;s the ability expand the component.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpdating a Template\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOn expanding a new template, you will come across a large text box, this box is where you\n            implement any css you want to be used across the site.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Templates/UpdateTemplateContent-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo save any CSS changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made within a template you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Save\u0026rdquo;\n \u003C/strong\u003Ebutton on the\n            relevant row. This will save any changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made to this template.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EDeleting a Template \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a template that you no longer use or need, then you click the \u0026ldquo;Delete\u0026rdquo; button that\n            will remove your template and its content from the UI.\n        \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Templates/DeleteTemplate-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
    ],
    "PageInfo": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Description": "How to access and manage the templates in the portal.",
        "Title": "Templates"
      }
    ],
    "ResourceKey": "Default"
  },
  {
    "Path": "Documentation/ContentManagement/AppManagement/Theming",
    "Name": "Theming",
    "ShowOnMenus": true,
    "Order": 70,
    "LastUpdated": "2026-07-21T17:12:54.504253\u002B01:00",
    "Layout": "Documentation",
    "Contents": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing Theme Management \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou Access this page through the App Management Tabs. From here you can manage what the current\n        app\u0026rsquo;s theme, this includes the logos that are displayed in the site\u0026rsquo;s header and the colours that are used\n        throughout the application.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you go to the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Theming\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/ThemeManagementUI-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere, the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Brand Logo\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is the logo that is displayed at the top left of the\n        screen and the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Project Logo\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is typically the logo of the project, for example, for this demo app this could\n        incorporate the\n        words \u0026ldquo;Corporate LinX Demo\u0026rdquo;. We also support having a background animation which is mostly visible on the Login\n        and Home pages of the site which can be uploaded by dragging and dropping your image from your local file\n        explorer to the upload box. You may also change the existing files in DMS by dragging and dropping a new image\n        over the previews. From this tab, you can also manage the themes that exist in the current application.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ECreating a Theme \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/ThemeGrid-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis grid is where you manage the themes that exist in the application, to create a new theme\n        you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button which will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/CreateThemeDialog-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECreating a new theme is simple as it only requires you to give it a name and click the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Confirm\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button. Creating a \u0026ldquo;Test\u0026rdquo; theme you can see that it\u0026rsquo;s added into the grid:\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/TestTheme-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpdating a Theme \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo update the theme that was just created, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Edit\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button on\n        the relevant row,\n        this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditThemeDialog-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EColours \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo understand what each of these colours represent, the dialog is broken down into two\n        sections, \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Base Colours\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Chart Colours\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditBaseColours-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Base Colours\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E section is where you set the \u0026ldquo;main\u0026rdquo; colours that are used\n        across the\n        application, most obviously, the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Primary\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E colour defines the colour of the header bar that\n        goes across the\n        screen and the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Secondary\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E colour defines the colour of any headings for charts or dialogs for\n        example. The\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Background\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E colour determines the colour of the background of the site as a whole. We allow\n        for two different\n        text colours so that they can be used in situations where the contrast maybe too low for the users reading it.\n        The\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Links\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E colour determines what colour any links within the portal will be displayed as and the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Margins\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E sets up\n        the value for the default margins across the portal, which determines how much spaces there is between the\n        components.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditChartColours-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Chart Colours\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E section is where you set up the colours for the charts\n        across the\n        application, ideally these should all be different colours and not similar shades of the same colour as this\n        will mean that the data displayed in chart format is more difficult to read.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo change any of the colours in this section of the dialog, you click onto the dropdown that\n        corresponds to the colour you want to edit, this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/ColourPicker-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe rectangles in the top right are there for previewing the colour you currently have\n        selected. You can change the colour by either using the colour picker using your cursor, or by entering a HEX\n        colour code which is often provided to you on a style sheet.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EFont \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Font\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab within this dialog displays something that looks\n        like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditFont-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Size\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E can be selected using the slider, as you can see in screenshot the\n        size is set to 11\n        px and the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Family\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E determines what font that\u0026rsquo;s used across the portal. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EBorder \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Border\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab within this dialog displays something that looks\n        like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditBorder-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Style\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Edropdown allows a default border style to be set across the\n        portal, these borders\n        will be displayed around every component that you see. It would be recommended to keep this value low at\n        potentially 1 or 2px which you can set with the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Width\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E slider below. The\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Colour\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E of these borders are\n        determined by the colour picker in this dialog. The \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Radius\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E sets the CSS property,\n        border-radius. this is what\n        determines how rounded the corners of the border are displayed, small values result in more pointed-looking\n        corners and higher values will make them much more rounded.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ENotifications \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Notifications\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab within this dialog displays something that\n        looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditNotifications-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis section of the dialog defines what colours the notifications appear are. These can be fully\n        customised using the colour pickers within this section, it\u0026rsquo;s important to ensure that the text colour isn\u0026rsquo;t too\n        dark or too light in comparison to the background colour as this would mean that the text is less readable and\n        users may have issues reading the description of the error they\u0026rsquo;ve received.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EShadows\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Shadows\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab within this dialog displays something that looks\n        like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditShadows-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Horizontal Offset\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E slider determines how far in pixels the shadow appears\n        to the left or\n        the right, the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Vertical Offset\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E defines how far in pixels the shadow appears to the top or the\n        bottom of the\n        container. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Blur Radius\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E determines how blurry the shadow appears, setting this to 0 will mean\n        that the shadow\n        will look like a solid black border. The higher this value is set to the further the colour is diffused across.\n        The \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Colour\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Eof this shadow can be set to whatever you want, however if you want it to look\n        like a more\n        \u0026ldquo;natural\u0026rdquo; shadow then this should be set to black or a dark grey colour.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EEtc \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u0026ldquo;Etc\u0026rdquo; tab within this dialog displays something that looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/EditThemeEtc-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Paint Login Mid\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E sets the login component on the login page of the portal\n        to be displayed\n        in the middle of the screen and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Paint Login Bottom\u0022\u003C/strong\u003E sets it such that the login component is\n        displayed at the\n        bottom of the page. It is supported such that we can use a flag or an image display to display what cultures can\n        be selected within the portal, this can be changed by selecting \u0026ldquo;Picture\u0026rdquo; in the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Culture Flag\n            Layout\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E dropdown.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo save any changes made within this dialog, you just click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Save\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button.\n        This will save\n        any changes to the application\u0026rsquo;s configuration and they should be now visible in the portal.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EDeleting a Theme \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou can delete a theme in the themes grid by clicking the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Delete\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button on the row of the\n        theme you want to delete.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Theming/DeleteTheme-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis will delete the theme from the application\u0026rsquo;s config and remove it from the grid.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
    ],
