      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing our Content Management System \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOur Content Management System (CMS) sits under the Admin tab as this is predominantly used by\n        admins. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOnce you have successfully logged into the portal, you can access the page by hovering over the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Admin\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button in the navigation bar and clicking \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Content Management\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you access the page, you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/PageSelector-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003ELike with DMS, when you first access this page, there appears to be nothing on it. However, as\n        you can see on the left, there\u0026rsquo;s a list of all the pages in the portal. To view a page\u0026rsquo;s content you select it\n        from the list. For example, expanding \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Documentation\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and then expanding \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Core\n Documentation\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003E then selecting\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Document Management System\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will bring up a page that looks something like this:\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/ContentArea-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis is an editable view of the page that is selected, you will notice that the right hand side\n        is an editable box that allows you to change any text on the page quickly and easily. There are also buttons on\n        the top that allow you to perform different actions on the page.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ESelect a Page\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis functionality is the same as that on the left hand menu - it allows you to select the page\n        you would like to edit. Clicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Select Page\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button will bring up a dialog that looks\n        like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/SelectPageDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022441\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you select a page on this dialog, it will load in an editable format allowing you to make\n        changes to it quickly and easily.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ECreating a Page \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ENew Root Page \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New Root Page\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button brings up a dialog that looks something\n        like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/NewPageDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022218\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEntering a name for your new page and clicking \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Create\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will create a new page\n        with that name\n        that is a root page, this means that it is typically a parent page that child pages will sit under. This means\n        that the path essentially becomes Parent. For example, App Management is a root page.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ENew Child Page \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New Child Page\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button brings up a dialog that looks\n        something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/NewChildPageDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022215\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEntering a name for your new page and clicking \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Create\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will create a new page\n        with that name\n        that is a \u0026ldquo;Child\u0026rdquo; of the page you\u0026rsquo;re editing. This means that the path essentially becomes Parent/Child. For\n        example, App Management is a child page of the Admin page.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EUpdating a Page \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EPage Properties \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EGeneral \u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Page Properties\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button brings up a dialog that looks\n        something like this:\u003C/p\u003Esrc=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/NewChildPageDialog-en.png\u0022 /\u0026gt;\n    \u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/PagePropertiesGeneral-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIn the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;General\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab contains the page\u0026rsquo;s general settings, including the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Layout\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E that the page\n        uses, \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Show on Menu\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E determines whether or not the page is shown in the navigation menu,\n        de-selecting this will\n        remove it from the navigation menu. The \u0026ldquo;Resource Key\u0026rdquo; field corresponds to the resource set you want to be used\n        on this page, for example domain-specific pages should use the matching domain resource key.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EInformation \u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIn the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Information\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab, you can manage a few things related to the page. You\n        can set up the\n        \u0026ldquo;Culture\u0026rdquo; which allows you to set the language of the page information, \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Title\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E this is the\n        title of the page,\n        you can create new rows in the grid that will allow you to set up different translations of the page\u0026rsquo;s title.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/PagePropertiesInformation-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EClicking on the \u003Cstrong\u003E \u0026ldquo;New\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003E will create a new row in the dialog, which you can fill\n        in with the\n        information you desire. For example, if you want to create a French translation for the page\u0026rsquo;s title, you\u0026rsquo;ll\n        select \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;French (France)\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003Efrom the drop down in the cultures column, and set the title to the\n        French translation\n        of \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Document Management System\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E. This means that when the culture is set to French in the\n        portal, the title will\n        be shown as the French translation set here.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/PagePropertiesEditInformation-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Description\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Keywords\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E columns aren\u0026rsquo;t required,\n        however if you wish to provided a description or any keywords that relate to the page you\u0026rsquo;re creating then they\n        can be filled in here. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ERoles \u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIn the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Roles\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab, you can manage what users can see the page you\u0026rsquo;ve created,\n        for example if\n        it\u0026rsquo;s only relevant for Administrators, then you would assign only that role to the page so that only\n        Administrators can view it. You can change these by selecting or de-selecting them in the grid.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/PagePropertiesRoles-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EContent Area \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAs you\u0026rsquo;re aware, the content area of the page, is an editable text box. When you click this, a\n        toolbar appears that allows you to add text as you would in word and control the formatting of it. The toolbar\n        looks something like this, and the icon in the top left of it allows you to freely move it around the screen for\n        ease of use.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/EditPageToolbar-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/TextStyleEditor-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis tool bar allows you to modify any content on the page, for example the \u003Cstrong\u003EB\u003C/strong\u003E\n button allows you\n        to set the selected text style to bold, \u003Cstrong\u003EI\u003C/strong\u003E allows you to set the selected text to be itallic and\n        \u003Cstrong\u003EU\u003C/strong\u003E allows you to\n        set whether or not you want that text to be displayed underlined.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/UndoRedoButtons-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe next two buttons that contain the arrows allow you to undo and redo any changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made\n        in the content. Allowing you to quickly revert any mistakes you may have made along the way. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/TextAlignButtons-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe group of three buttons following the undo and redo buttons allow you to control the text\n        alignment on the page. You may recognise these things from programs like Microsoft word. The left one allows you\n        to align text to the left-hand side of the page, the middle button allows you to centre-align the content on the\n        page and the third button allows you to right-align the text.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/BulletPointButton-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe first button of the next group allows you to embed a link on the page, clicking it opens a\n        dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/LinkEmbedDialog-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Web address\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E box need to be populated with the link you want on the page,\n        the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Text\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E box\n        needs to be populated with the text you want to replace the link with (ideally this needs to be relevant to\n        where the link will take you). \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;ToolTip\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will provide any extra information to the user when\n        the link is hovered\n        over. Selecting the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Open link in new window\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will ensure that when the link is clicked, it\n        will open it up in a\n        new window as opposed to directing them away from the page that they are looking at. To confirm your choices and\n        to embed the link onto the page within the content, click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Insert\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/ImageEmbedButton-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe next, non-greyed out button is used to embed an image on the page, clicking this button\n        opens a dialog that looks something like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/ImageEmbedDialog-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Web address\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is the link where the image can be found, for example, to get\n        an image from DMS in the current portal, this link will need to look something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E [app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/image.png \u003C/pre\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Alternate text\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E field needs to be filled in with a brief description of\n        the image, as this\n        will be displayed if the image can\u0026rsquo;t be displayed for some reason. The \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;width\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;height\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E fields need to be\n        populated with the desired width and height (in px) of the image you\u0026rsquo;re placing.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/CreateTableButton-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis button allows you to create a table in the content area, clicking on this button gives you\n        a dialog that looks something like this: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/CreateTableDialog-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you hover over the boxes, you will see a different level of highlighting, you can use this\n        to determine the size of the table that you want. By highlighting the appropriate number of columns and rows and\n        simply just clicking. This will then create an empty table in the content area which you can then add content\n        to. However, if you wish to have more control over the table\u0026rsquo;s styling you may want to create your table using\n        the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Table Wizard\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E. Clicking this button will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ETable Tab \u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/TableWizardTable-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Width\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E here determines the total width of the table in px, and\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Height\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E determines the total\n        height of the table. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Columns\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is used to set the total number of columns in the table and\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Rows\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will be the\n        total number of rows. The \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Cell Spacing\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E refers to the amount of space you want there to be\n        between cells (in\n        px) in the table and the \u003Cstrong\u003ECell Padding\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\u0026ldquo; relates to the padding (white space) around any content\n        within the cells\n        in px. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Alignment\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E allows you to set up how you want the text to be aligned within the table\u0026rsquo;s\n        cells.\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Background\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E allows you to select a preferred background colour. The \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;CSS\n Class\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E field can be populated with a\n        known CSS class, which may define the \u0026ldquo;default\u0026rdquo; table formatting in the portal you\u0026rsquo;re in, setting an\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;ID\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E will\n        allow you to easily select this element using CSS to apply any specific styling you want to it.\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Border\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E accepts\n        a value for the border width (in px) in the text box, this determines the \u0026ldquo;weight\u0026rdquo;/thickness of it. The colour\n        picker next to this field allows you to specify a preferred border colour for the table you\u0026rsquo;re creating.\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Border\n Style\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E allows you to specify the style of border you\u0026rsquo;d like, whether you\u0026rsquo;d like it to be dotted,\n        solid or dashed\n        for example.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ECell Tab \u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/TableWizardCell-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Select All Cells\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is selected, any changes made and confirmed within\n        this dialog will be\n        applied to all cells within the table you\u0026rsquo;re creating. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Width\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\u0026gt; and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Height\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\n here apply to the cells only and not\n        to the table as a whole. This is useful when you only want one or a few cells within the table to have differing\n        styles. All of the styles that can be set in this tab apply only to the cell you\u0026rsquo;ve selected and not to the\n        whole table like in the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Table\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E tab. When \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Wrap text\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is not selected, it will\n        mean that the text does not wrap\n        onto new lines when reaching the limits of the cell size.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EAccessibility Tab \u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/TableWizardAccessibility-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThese settings enhance the table\u0026rsquo;s accessibility, the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Header Rows\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E and\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Header Columns\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\n determine how many header rows and columns there are in the defined table. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Caption\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E should\n        provide the user\n        with a concise explanation of the information that is displayed in the table you\u0026rsquo;re creating. The\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Associate\n headers\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003E determine links between the header columns and rows and how you expect them to be linked\n        to one\n        another.\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/TextHierarchy-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe dropdown with the text \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Heading 1\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E allows you to set the \u0026ldquo;tag\u0026rdquo; of the\n        content, for example\n        \u0026ldquo;Heading 1\u0026rdquo; would be representative of a main heading and the content would usually be contained in\n    \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ehtml tags. Setting this to \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Paragraph\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E would ensure that your text is the same style as\n    typical main body\n    text.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/FontColouring-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe first colour picker allows you to select what colour you would like the font to be\n        displayed as and the second colour picker enables you to specify a highlight colour, if you want the text to be\n        highlighted.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/ViewSourceButton-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe final button in the toolbar is the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;View Source\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button, when you click\n        this it comes up\n        with an editor that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/ViewSourceDialog-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis editor is particularly useful if you would like to input content on the site in the form\n        of HTML and it is where it can be placed such that the content within it is displayed on the page you\u0026rsquo;re\n        editing.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EDeleting a Page \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a page from the system, you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Delete Page\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button from the toolbar at the top\n        of the page. This will remove the selected page from the system and it will no longer be visible in the UI. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/CMS/DeletePage-en.png\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
    ],
