  {
    "Path": "Documentation/Mail/MailManagement",
    "Name": "Mail Management",
    "ShowOnMenus": true,
    "Order": 10,
    "LastUpdated": "2026-07-21T17:13:11.6341619\u002B01:00",
    "Layout": "Documentation",
    "Contents": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Name": "body",
        "Html": "\u003Cheader class=\u0022docs-page-header\u0022\u003E\u003Ch1\u003E[page[title]]\u003C/h1\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[page[description]]\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/header\u003E\u003Cdiv class=\u0022documentation\u0022\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EAccessing Mail Management \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou access this functionality through the App Management Tabs. From here, you can see any\n        emails that have been sent from our system. These could be password reset emails, registration emails or just\n        the usual registration emails.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EThe UI\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhen you access the mail management tab, you\u0026rsquo;re greeted with something that looks like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/MailManagementGrid-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere, you would see any emails that were due to be sent out. As this is our demo system there\n        are currently none as not many people use the site from a day to day basis.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EHistory Tab\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIn the history tab, you can view any emails that have been sent out by our system previously and\n        it looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/HistoryTab-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe columns show: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESubject - the reason why the email was sent, \u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EFrom - where the email was sent from, \u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ETo - the email address it was sent to, \u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESent On - the date that the email was sent out to the user. \u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003EExpanding one of these rows will display the content of the email that was sent out to the user\n        at that time.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EMail Server Tab \u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThis tab is for configuring the mail accounts that the app can use to send emails out.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/MailServerTab-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Ch2\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ECreating a Mail Server\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo set up a new in this UI, you click on the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;New\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E button in the header bar of\n        the mail server grid. Clicking this will bring up a dialog that looks something like this:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/CreateMailServerDialog-en.png\u0022 height=\u0022353\u0022 style=\u0022display:block;\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHere, \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Name\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E represents the name you want to give to your mail server and you\n        may want it to be\n        relevant to that app you are in. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;User\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E is the email address you wish the emails to be sent\n        from and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Password\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\n is the password for that email account. \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Host\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Eis the name of the host which is used to send\n        emails and \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Port\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E\n is the communication endpoint which is usually set to 25. In the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Enable SSL\u0026rdquo;\u003C/strong\u003E box, you can\n        either set this to\n        true or false, as you can see it\u0026rsquo;s set as true be default.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/TestMailServer-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFor now, I have created a test mail server. On this row you can see that there are save and\n        delete functions.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EUpdating a Mail Server \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou edit mail servers by just clicking onto the field you want to change. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/UpdateMailServer-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOnce you\u0026rsquo;ve made any changes you want, you click the \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Save\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Ebutton on the\n        corresponding grid row and any changes you\u0026rsquo;ve made will be saved.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EDeleting a Mail Server \u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo delete a mail server that you no longer want to use in this app, then you click the\n        \u003Cstrong\u003E\u0026ldquo;Remove\u0026rdquo; \u003C/strong\u003Ebutton that will remove your schedule and its content from the UI.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cimg src=\u0022[app[root]]Api/DMS/Content/Documentation/Core Documentation/App Management/Mail Management/DeleteMailServer-en.png\u0022 /\u003E\u003C/div\u003E"
      }
    ],
    "PageInfo": [
      {
        "CultureId": "",
        "Description": "How to access and manage the mail sending in the portal.",
        "Title": "Mail Management"
      }
    ],
    "ResourceKey": "Default"
  },
